    "validationNotes": "The Cu-first Redlich-Kister coefficients are obtained by transforming the published Ag-first convention. A numerical common-tangent calculation using the full liquid and FCC models gives a eutectic temperature of approximately 1053.0 K (779.9 C), consistent with the NIST assessment value 779.1 C. The three coexistence compositions are also consistent with the NIST invariant-equilibrium composition to within the expected numerical/model-reference precision."
